# Vercel serves ONLY the static frontend. The Python API runs in a container (Dockerfile).
#
# Without this file Vercel finds requirements.txt and app.py — app.py is one of the
# filenames it treats as a Python entrypoint — builds a serverless function, and the
# installed dependencies reach ~1 GB against a 500 MB bundle limit. Hiding the Python
# side from the build is what keeps this a static deployment.
*.py
requirements.txt
Dockerfile
models/
*.command
README.md
.gitignore
